# Frontend build-time configuration.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, so never put
# a secret in this file — everything here ships inside the JS bundle.
#
# LEAVE VITE_API_URL UNSET for the single-origin setup (recommended): the app
# then calls same-origin /api, which the host rewrites to the backend — no CORS,
# and the backend host never enters the bundle, so changing the domain needs no
# rebuild. `npm run dev` and `./scripts/serve-local.sh` both proxy /api locally.
#
# Only set it when the API is on a different origin and there is no rewrite:
# VITE_API_URL="https://api.your-domain.example/api"
